  "html": "<p class=\"\">My first generative art bot — <a href=\"https://x.com/417am1975\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"external-link group inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400\" data-preview-url=\"https://x.com/417am1975\">@417am1975</a>, running since 2017. It picks a random art script, renders a piece with node-canvas, and tweets it, on the hour, on its own.</p>\n<p class=\"\">This was my first generative art bot, and boy did he make some dope shit. It came from node-canvas tick-generations.</p>\n<p class=\"\">I like it as an artifact of how I was using the robots to make art before AI, and how that changes my perspective on things as a computer-aided artist.</p>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"Twitter Artbot — generative piece 1\" class=\"\">\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/twitter-artbot/piece-01.png\" alt=\"Twitter Artbot — generative piece 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/projects/twitter-artbot/piece-01.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/projects/twitter-artbot/piece-01.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/projects/twitter-artbot/piece-01.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/projects/twitter-artbot/piece-01.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"Twitter Artbot — generative piece 1\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" style=\"--splay-rot:-0.95deg;\" data-dimensions=\"1080×1080\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm img-splay aspect-square w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<figcaption class=\"\">Twitter Artbot — generative piece 1</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"Twitter Artbot — generative piece 2\" class=\"\">\n<img